### Cafe Management System - API Test File
### Use this file with REST Client extension in VS Code or import to Postman/Insomnia

### Variables (Update these as needed)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### ==========================================
### HEALTH CHECK
### ==========================================

### Check if server is running
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

### ==========================================
### AUTHENTICATION TESTS
### ==========================================

### 1. Register a new customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "1234567890",
  "role": "customer"
}

### 2. Register a staff member
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Staff",
  "email": "jane.staff@cafe.com",
  "password": "staff123",
  "phone": "0987654321",
  "role": "staff"
}

### 3. Register an admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Admin User",
  "email": "admin@cafe.com",
  "password": "admin123",
  "phone": "5555555555",
  "role": "admin"
}

### 4. Login with customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Login with staff
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.staff@cafe.com",
  "password": "staff123"
}

### 6. Login with admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@cafe.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 7. Get user profile (requires token)
### First login and copy the token to the @token variable above
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ==========================================
### ERROR CASES
### ==========================================

### Login with wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Login with non-existent user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "notexist@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Try to access protected route without token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Content-Type: application/json

### Try to access protected route with invalid token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_here
